From bb6f9a55f483be47c561c5a3dd8496c6653c5f77 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Viet Hung Nguyen <hvn@calif.io>
Date: Tue, 18 Aug 2026 19:12:53 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] fix: Do not fabricate a value when the input runs out
 mid-datum

Three arms of `decode_internal` treated `ErrorKind::UnexpectedEof` as a value
rather than as an error, so a truncated buffer decoded successfully into data
that was never on the wire:

  Schema::Boolean  ->  Ok(Value::Null)
  Schema::String   ->  Ok(Value::Null)
  Schema::Union    ->  Ok(Value::Union(0, Box::new(Value::Null)))

None of the three inhabits the schema it was decoded under. `null` is not a
value of `boolean` or of `string`, and branch 0 of a union is only `null` when
the union happens to declare it first, so `["int"]` yielded a union whose
payload had the wrong type. A record of two booleans decoded from zero bytes
into a record of two nulls, with an Ok status and no indication that nothing had
been read. Apache Avro C++ reports "EOF reached" for every one of these.

All three now propagate the io error. `Schema::Null` still decodes from an empty
buffer, which is correct: a `null` datum occupies zero bytes, so the fix could
not be "reject an empty buffer".

This is not additive for existing consumers, unlike the two settings-based
patches. `test_from_avro_datum_with_union_to_struct` relied on the union arm
directly: its payload encodes two of the record's five fields and let the three
trailing unions decode from nothing, described in the test as simulating missing
keys. Truncation is not the same thing as a writer that lacked those fields,
which is what schema resolution is for, so the test now asserts the error and
gained a companion payload with all five fields encoded. It still covers what it
was written for, a key absent from the target struct, via the field the struct
omits.

Verified on apache-avro 0.21 with the non-UTF-8 and uuid patches applied:
`cargo test -p apache-avro --features derive` goes from 558 to 562, the four
tests this adds. `cargo fmt --check` clean, and clippy reports nothing in
`decode.rs` or `reader.rs`.
---
 avro/src/decode.rs | 154 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++-------------------
 avro/src/reader.rs |  13 +++-
 2 files changed, 102 insertions(+), 65 deletions(-)

